    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-19T21:31:05+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T21:31:05+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T11:01:05Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T11:01:05Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system in the Bight will drift southeast as the associated trough crosses South Australia overnight and clears to the east by Friday. A weak high pressure system will then move across southern SA from Friday afternoon. A trough and cold front will then move into the west from Saturday evening and cross the rest of SA on Sunday. A high will then push in behind the front and will move across the Bight early next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-19T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers east of Leigh Creek, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding north of Leigh Creek. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower near the eastern border, most likely in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding east of Leigh Creek. Winds northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the middle of the day then tending south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 35 to 40.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly in the morning then tending northwest to northeasterly in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 26 with daytime temperatures reaching 35 to 41.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Yunta in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of raised dust north of Leigh Creek in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Leigh Creek in the afternoon and evening. Winds northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the day then tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to 22 to 29 with daytime temperatures reaching 39 to 45.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Leigh Creek in the afternoon. Winds southerly 30 to 45 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 27 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
